aiproof (0.1.19) unstable; urgency=medium

  * OpenAI-compatible endpoints accept a base URL again. Local servers
    (Lemonade, LM Studio, vLLM, LiteLLM, llama.cpp) document a base like
    http://host:8020/v1, but the request used the configured endpoint
    verbatim and POSTed to /v1 itself, which answers 404. Both the base and
    the full .../chat/completions form now work, matching the leniency the
    Ollama branch already had.
  * "List" works for OpenAI-compatible providers, not just Ollama: they all
    expose /v1/models. A 401/403 now says to set the provider's API key
    instead of surfacing a raw HTTP error. Formats with no listing API say
    so plainly.

 -- Ed Watson <edmundwatson@gmail.com>  Wed, 14 Oct 2026 20:45:00 +0200

